For linear maps $T, S: V -> W$ and scalars $alpha, beta$, the linear combination $alpha T + beta S: V -> W$ defined by
$ (alpha T + beta S)(vb(x)) = alpha T(vb(x)) + beta S(vb(x)) $
is again a linear map. For $T: V -> W$ and $S: U -> V$, the composition is a linear map $T compose S: U -> W$ defined by
$ (T compose S)(vb(x)) = T(S(vb(x))). $
